The wind off the Azure Sea always carried the scent of salt and forgotten gold. Elara hugged her shawl tighter, watching the sails of the passing merchant ships. They looked rich and oblivious, sailing into a life she wasn't a part of. Her ship, the *Wayward Star*, was built for speed and whispers, not for grand trade routes. Today, they were near the Serpent's Coil—a patch of water rumored to hide more than just coral reefs. Below the waves, the maps hinted at a civilization that predated the known world, ruled by magic and shadow. Elara felt the familiar pull, a siren song of adventure mixed with desperate necessity. She had to find the key, the forgotten artifact her grandmother had mentioned, before the Crimson Tide washed away any trace of it. The coast ahead was jagged, a promise of trouble and magnificent secrets.